AWS
1.What is EC2?
1.EC2 stands for Elastic compute cloud.
2.It is AWS virtual server which have computing power.
3.You can launch a server in minutes ,use it, shutdown it without purchasing and
managing physical hardware.
4.Billing is based on usage (pay as you go)
per hour/ per second depending on the instance type and OS.

2.Application and OS Images (Amazon Machine Image-AMI)
1.AMI is a pre -built template that contains OS, software and server configuration.
2.Every EC2 instance is created from an AMI.

3.You can create a custom AMI from a configured instance called a "Golden Image" used to launch a pre-configured
EC2 instance.

3.Instance type.
[Family][Generation][Size]
1.It determines the hardware profile vCPU, RAM and network.
2.t3 = General purpose  (Development, Testing, Learning , low-traffic apps)
3.c5 = Compute optimized (ML mode training , batch-processing)
4.r5 = Memory optimized
5.m5 = Balanced compute (production application)

4.Purchasing option.
1.On-Demand (DIs) : pay per hour/second . no upfront cost.
2.Reserved instance (RIs) : Commit 1 or 3 year , up 72% cheaper ,best for steady
3.Spot instances (SIs) : 90 % cheaper ,Use unused compute instance but AWS can terminate with 2- minutes notice.
4.Dedicated host : A physical server dedicated to your account for software licences
(HIPAA,PCI-DSS)

5.Security Groups.
1.Acts as a virtual firewall at the instance level.
2.Controls inbound and outbound traffic using rules.
3.Statefull : If inbound traffic is allow the response is automatically permitted
(Rule only allow , cannot deny.)
4.Multiple Security Groups (SG) are attached to one instance.

6.ENI (Elastic Network Interface)
7.ELASTIC IP (Static IP)